From: System Electronics
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: stop the source before disabling

The controller is shut down while the DPI in front of it is still
scanning. That window corrupts the input FIFO, and on the next enable
the video stream generator comes up and immediately reports a missing
HSYNC: the panel stays dark and nothing short of a reboot clears it.
The J721E TRM start-up procedure, 12.6.5.7.3, states the requirement in
both directions, and only the enable half was being met.

Measured on this board, same build and same parameters: 12 pipeline
exits in the current order, all of them dark and each needing a reboot;
10 exits with the source stopped 50 ms first, all clean, no reboot.

The DPI exposes no status bit saying it has stopped, so the wait is
blind. It takes up to 13 ms to stop, 50 ms is the value that was
measured good, and the extra black is accepted. source_stop_wait_ms set
to 0 makes this inert.

The watchdog has to be disarmed across the whole shutdown, not just
scheduled off: the generator is starved on purpose during the wait, and
a watchdog that notices would turn VID_EN back on in the middle of the
sequence. It already stops at the top of disable; the confirmation step
now rechecks before restarting, because confirming takes longer than a
frame and a disable can begin inside it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform workaround]

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <video/mipi_display.h>
 
 #include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/hailo-drm.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
@@ -746,6 +747,10 @@
 module_param(vsg_watchdog_gave_up, uint, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(vsg_watchdog_gave_up, "Times the watchdog stopped retrying until the next enable");
 
+static unsigned int vsg_watchdog_during_disable;
+module_param(vsg_watchdog_during_disable, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(vsg_watchdog_during_disable, "Restarts dropped because a disable was already running");
+
 /*
  * A healthy generator drops VSG_RUNNING for about 0.3 ms once per frame, so
  * one reading is never enough: confirm over more than a frame.
@@ -793,6 +798,11 @@
 		return;
 
 	if (cdns_dsi_vsg_broken(dsi)) {
+		if (!dsi->vsg_enabled) {
+			vsg_watchdog_during_disable++;
+			return;
+		}
+
 		cdns_dsi_vsg_restart(dsi, fast ? vsg_watchdog_fast_ms :
 						 vsg_watchdog_pause_ms);
 		if (fast)
@@ -804,6 +814,16 @@
 		 * The first restart after the DPI was reprogrammed often fails
 		 * again after about 18 ms: look once more before counting it.
 		 */
+		/*
+		 * Confirming takes more than a frame, and a disable can start in
+		 * the middle of it: the generator is starved on purpose there, so
+		 * restarting it would fight the shutdown.
+		 */
+		if (!dsi->vsg_enabled) {
+			vsg_watchdog_during_disable++;
+			return;
+		}
+
 		if (!cdns_dsi_vsg_broken(dsi)) {
 			dsi->vsg_fail_streak = 0;
 			vsg_watchdog_retry_streak = 0;
@@ -846,6 +866,10 @@
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dsi->vsg_work);
 }
 
+static unsigned int source_stop_wait_ms = 50;
+module_param(source_stop_wait_ms, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(source_stop_wait_ms, "Ms to let the DPI stop before shutting the controller down, 0 disables");
+
 static unsigned int disable_wait_ms = 50;
 module_param(disable_wait_ms, uint, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(disable_wait_ms, "Max ms to wait at disable for the video stream generator to stop");
@@ -863,6 +887,17 @@
 
 	cdns_dsi_vsg_watchdog_stop(dsi);
 
+	/*
+	 * The controller has to be shut down after its source has stopped. With
+	 * the source still scanning, the input FIFO is corrupted on the way down
+	 * and the generator comes back reporting a missing HSYNC, which nothing
+	 * short of a reboot clears. Stop the DPI first, then wait: it exposes no
+	 * status bit to poll, so the wait is blind, and 50 ms is the value that
+	 * was measured good.
+	 */
+	if (source_stop_wait_ms && !hailo_dpi_stop_scanout())
+		msleep(source_stop_wait_ms);
+
 	val = readl(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_DATA_CTL);
 	val &= ~(IF_VID_SELECT_MASK | IF_VID_MODE | VID_EN | HOST_EOT_GEN |
 		 DISP_EOT_GEN);
